CAT = "phrebResa"; SEG = "RSA"
Q = [
("Under R.A. 9646, a real estate broker is a duly registered and licensed:",
 "Natural person", ["Corporation", "Partnership", "Cooperative"],
 "Section 3 defines the real estate broker as a duly registered and licensed natural person who acts as agent of a party in a real estate transaction for a fee or commission."),
("A real estate salesperson under R.A. 9646 performs service:",
 "For a licensed broker", ["Independently for any client", "For the Board directly", "Only for developers"],
 "Section 3 defines the salesperson as a duly accredited natural person who performs service for, and on behalf of, a registered and licensed real estate broker."),
("Under R.A. 9646, an accredited salesperson who helped close a sale may demand a commission only from:",
 "The supervising broker", ["The buyer directly", "The seller directly", "Any party who agrees to pay in writing"],
 "Section 31 bars a salesperson from receiving or demanding any fee or commission from anyone other than the licensed broker who has direct control and supervision over him or her."),
("A salesperson signs a contract to sell for a lot alone, without the supervising broker. Under R.A. 9646, this is:",
 "Not allowed", ["Allowed for small lots", "Allowed with a notary", "Allowed if the buyer agrees"],
 "Salespersons cannot by themselves be signatories to a written agreement involving a real estate transaction unless their supervising broker also signs it (Section 31)."),
("A realty corporation must have at least one licensed broker for every:",
 "20 accredited salespersons", ["5 accredited salespersons", "50 accredited salespersons", "100 accredited salespersons"],
 "Section 32 of R.A. 9646 requires at least one licensed real estate broker for every twenty accredited salespersons in a partnership or corporation engaged in real estate service."),
("Which person is exempt from R.A. 9646 when selling a lot?",
 "An owner selling his own lot", ["A developer selling its units", "An unpaid agent's salesperson", "A broker on suspension"],
 "Section 28 exempts a person who directly sells his or her own property, except real estate developers. Developers must market through licensed brokers and accredited salespersons."),
("An attorney-in-fact who sells her brother's house is exempt from R.A. 9646 only if she:",
 "Takes no compensation", ["Is a lawyer", "Is a member of the same family", "Sells within a year"],
 "Section 28(d) exempts a duly constituted attorney-in-fact for sale, mortgage or lease only when the service is performed without any form of compensation."),
("Licensed brokers and private appraisers must post professional indemnity insurance or a cash or surety bond, renewable every:",
 "Three years", ["Year", "Five years", "Ten years"],
 "Section 26 of R.A. 9646 requires the bond or professional indemnity insurance, renewable every three years, in an amount set by the Board."),
("On documents a broker signs in practice, R.A. 9646 requires the broker to indicate:",
 "Registration, PTR and APO numbers", ["Home address and age", "TIN of the buyer", "Bank account and home address details"],
 "Section 38 requires the certificate of registration and ID number, the Professional Tax Receipt number and the APO receipt number, with dates of issue and validity."),
("A broker hires a salesperson who has no accreditation from the Board. Under R.A. 9646 the broker:",
 "Violates the law", ["Is excused if unaware", "Only needs to warn them", "May pay them in cash"],
 "Section 31 makes a broker guilty of violating the Act for employing or using a salesperson who has not first secured the required accreditation."),
("A revoked certificate of registration may be reinstated by the Board no earlier than:",
 "Two years after revocation", ["Six months after revocation", "One year after revocation", "Five years after revocation"],
 "Section 21 allows reinstatement after two years from revocation, on application, compliance with CPE units and for proper reasons."),
("Under R.A. 9646, the penalty when a violation is committed by an unlicensed practitioner is:",
 "Double the regular penalty", ["Half the regular penalty", "A warning only", "The same penalty that a licensee gets"],
 "Section 39 doubles the fine and imprisonment when the violation is committed by an unlicensed real estate service practitioner."),
]
